# Rendering reads this file instead of the renderer's ~/.Rprofile (R uses a
# .Rprofile in the working directory in place of the user's). It keeps the
# rendered pages independent of anyone's personal settings: no seeds, digits or
# other options leak in, so the page prints what a fresh R session prints and
# the downloadable code gives the same numbers for readers. Seeds are set in the
# lesson code itself. (Ben's ~/.Rprofile set digits = 2 and set.seed(1234); 09-24.)
invisible(NULL)
